# L §5.7, L §8 R1 and Refusals outrank holes (tally 2.1.8 R11, #180): a binding on a hole day reads its where for every
# thing that could be in it, so a where that refuses (w[p] / zero) refuses the count (c1) and the sum (c4), with the
# where's code, outranking the day's hole; the where on a known day refuses alike (c2). Twins: no where, the day's hole
# (c0); a where no thing passes, 0 (c3). 2.1.7's refcore printed the day's hole for c1 and c4.
=== m.tally
model hh
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
kind persons
input dd: date
input zero: num
input w[p in persons]: num

version v1
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ola] lives 1990-02-01..
  persons + [jan] lives 1991-02-01..
  dd = ?"which day" "s"
  zero = 0 "s"
  w[ola] = 2 "s"
  w[jan] = 3 "s"
ask c0: count(p in persons on dd)
ask c1: count(p in persons on dd where w[p] / zero > 1)
ask c2: count(p in persons on 2026-03-01 where w[p] / zero > 1)
ask c3: count(p in persons on dd where w[p] > w[ola] + w[jan])
ask c4: sum(w[p] for p in persons on dd where w[p] / zero > 1)
=== expect
c0: ?"which day" (dd)
  cut 2026-10-20
c1: refused: RUN-DIV division by zero
  cut 2026-10-20
c2: refused: RUN-DIV division by zero
  cut 2026-10-20
c3: 0
  cut 2026-10-20
c4: refused: RUN-DIV division by zero
  cut 2026-10-20
